---
// The four features DRO-102 names. Card copy is condensed from the 8e7af91
// index.html text; it makes no claim that page did not already make.
---
<h2>What it does</h2>
<div class="features">

  <div class="feature-card">
    <h3>Look up any skater&rsquo;s scores by name</h3>
    <p>
      Type a skater&rsquo;s name and Sk8tics finds their results across Skate
      Ontario competitions and Skate Canada&rsquo;s national events in seconds
      rather than an afternoon of opening PDFs.
    </p>
    <p>
      Import one and the whole protocol comes across: base values, every
      judge&rsquo;s mark, the program components with their factors, and the
      deduction with its reason.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-card">
    <h3>Compare, your last competition or another skater&rsquo;s</h3>
    <p>
      Put two skates side by side: your last competition against this one to
      see your own progress, or your skate against another skater&rsquo;s or the
      winner&rsquo;s from the same segment.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Progress chart puts a season of competitions on one date axis, so the
      trend and the time since the last one both show.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-card">
    <h3>A practice log, with your coach&rsquo;s notes</h3>
    <p>
      Four marks per element &mdash; landed, missed, fell, not attempted. No
      typing on cold hands. History shows the check rate for each element week
      by week, so an element that is quietly slipping is plain to see.
    </p>
    <p>
      A coach scores a run-through against the current ISU scale of values and
      writes a note against each element.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-card wide">
    <h3>Planned against what the panel called</h3>
    <p>
      Programs hold each season of planned elements. Record what a panel
      actually called against what the programme planned.
    </p>

    <!-- A real row from a real sheet. Pre-Novice Free Dance, 2026 Ontario
         Provincials: a dance spin planned at level 3 that came back basic. -->
    <section class="sheet" aria-label="Example of a recorded competition element">
      <div class="sheet-head">
        <span>Free Dance &middot; element 3</span>
        <span>Pre-Novice</span>
      </div>
      <div class="el">
        <div class="el-line">
          <span class="el-pos">3</span>
          <span class="el-was">DSp3</span>
          <span class="el-arrow">&rarr;</span>
          <span class="el-now">DSpB</span>
          <span class="el-spacer"></span>
          <span class="el-base">1.80</span>
          <span class="el-goe">&minus;0.27</span>
          <span class="el-score">1.53</span>
        </div>
        <div class="judges" aria-label="Judges' grades of execution">
          <span class="hi">0</span><span>0</span><span>&minus;1</span>
          <span class="lo">&minus;2</span><span class="lo">&minus;2</span>
        </div>
        <div class="coach-note">
          <span class="who">Coach&rsquo;s note</span>
          Short rotations coming out of the change of edge &mdash; you had the
          position, you just left it early. Hold two more before the exit.
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="stamp">
      Planned level 3, called basic. That costs 1.20 in base value before a judge
      marks anything &mdash; and the note is why it happened.
    </p>
  </div>

</div>
